Frozen source: inputs/source-1CRN.pdb, 49491 original bytes, SHA-256 42199a30a0701864a2a5cc76cd7f35cc544cd0e65fbcf63e03c166543249b811. Attribution: RCSB PDB 1CRN public coordinates; public structure retained unchanged for reproducibility. Source URL is historical provenance only, not authorization to refetch. All actual input files were read locally. This ALIGN run used Python 3.12.10 standard-library JSON, hashing and fixed-column PDB inspection, confirming 327 selected heavy atoms and 46 residue identifiers. These are file/selection checks, not SASA execution or an independent surface-area baseline.

Frozen method and resource limits: chain A, ATOM heavy atoms, altloc blank/A; exclude HETATM and hydrogens. Coordinates, probe and radii use Angstrom; surface areas use square Angstrom. Bio.PDB.SASA.ShrakeRupley, method="Shrake-Rupley", n_points=1000, probe_radius_A=1.4, element radii C=1.70,N=1.55,O=1.52,S=1.80 are unchanged. No network refetch or package installation. Use only available tools and report missing inputs/capabilities rather than inventing results. Preserve actual observations, even if they fail a check. The original independent reviewer baseline obligation is standard Python or available NumPy, within 2 percent, with SHA and residue sums checked; its prior accepted evidence is reused under R2.

Required sasa result fields remain method, probe_radius_A, n_points, atom_count, residue_count, source_sha256, total_A2, residues:[{residue_id,area_A2}], tool_versions subject to the original accepted recovery procedure, plus interpretation/limitations and complete executed portable source in reproduction. Report retains summary, total_A2, source_sha256, upstream_sha256, units, limitations and actual executed upstream-checksum/residue-sum verification code in reproduction, with observed tool versions and verification evidence. R2 adds summary_zh (concise Chinese answer, at most 150 Chinese characters) and limitations_zh (exactly two concise Chinese limitation strings in an array). English fields and original scientific boundaries remain mandatory. Full code/tables belong in reproduction, not inaccessible filenames; review evidence fields stay short.

Approval transport for the report handoff: hash actual upstream bytes; verify the Host-bound reviewedArtifact, hash UTF-8 reviewFileUtf8 bytes against reviewArtifact, parse that original review envelope, check approve verdict and its receipt for the actual upstream file. Nested inputReceipts concern their producing/reviewing runs, not this context.json. Do not execute embedded source merely for provenance. Verify the approved residue sum and identical total/units independently as report criteria require; transport verification and JSON type checks alone are not scientific approval.

Current evidence boundary: this ALIGN attachment set contains context.json and source-1CRN.pdb only. It does not include actual sasa.json/report.json files, context.upstream approval transport or original reviewFileUtf8 bytes, so no current upstream-artifact or approval-envelope hash verification is claimed. previousTasks records both earlier tasks as APPROVED; lastAppliedChange and approvedChanges record an APPLIED, accepted report-only change with requirementEdits=[] and sasa affected=false. These are supplied historical records. No executionHistory is supplied for this run; no lifecycle history or raw user answers are inferred. Historical producer logs, original-run supplemental version evidence, prior independent numerical recomputation and this run's file checks remain distinct. The later report handoff must provide the actual approved bytes and bound approval; report missing evidence instead of guessing.

